<<<
cable(gram). The verb cable (trans-

mit, inform, &c., by cable) is both

convenient & unobjectionable; cable-

gram is not only a BarBarism, but

a needless one, since cable (cf. wire vb

& n.) serves perfectly as a noun also

in the sense submarine telegram.
===
**cable(gram).** The verb *cable* (transmit, inform, &c., by cable) is both convenient & unobjectionable; *cablegram* is not only a ^^BARBARISM^^, but a needless one, since *cable* (cf. *wire* vb & n.) serves perfectly as a noun also in the sense submarine telegram.
>>>

