<<<
cadi. Pronounce kah‘di; pl. cadis. cadre, being an established mili technicality, should be anglicized in sound & pronounced kah‘der, in pl. kah’derz; the French pronunciation is especially inconvenient in words much used in the plural. caesura. See TECHNICAL TERMS. café is naturalized in the sense coffee-house or restaurant; in the sense coffee it is a FRENCH worpD. café chantant, café noir. See caffeine. Pronounce k&’ftin,
===
**cadi.** Pronounce kah'dī; pl. *cadis*.

**cadre**, being an established military technicality, should be anglicized in sound & pronounced kah'd*er*, in pl. kah'd*erz*; the French pronunciation is especially inconvenient in words much used in the plural.

**caduceus.** Pl. *-cei*; see ^^-US^^.

**caecum, Caesar, caesious, caesura, &c.** See ^^Æ, Œ^^.

**caesura.** See ^^TECHNICAL TERMS^^.

**café** is naturalized in the sense coffee-house or restaurant; in the sense coffee it is a ^^FRENCH WORD^^.

**café chantant, café noir.** See ^^FRENCH WORDS^^.

**caffeine.** Pronounce kă'ffīn.


